whelk (0.22.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The lock screen no longer rejects every password when the optional
    /etc/pam.d/whelk-lock service is absent.  whelk now chooses the login
    stack in that case, as swaylock does; an installed whelk-lock stack still
    fails closed.
  * The password entry receives window-level keyboard focus when a lock
    surface maps and after a retry re-enables it.
  * PAM ECHO_ON prompts receive the account name, and the headless
    integration suite covers both the dedicated and login PAM stacks.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:41:05 +0100

whelk (0.21.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The screen locker keeps the compositor lock across SIGTERM, survives a
    primary-output replacement, and persists its retry backoff across a
    restart.
  * Suspend, VT switches and logind IdleHint transitions now request the lock.
  * The headless integration suite covers PAM backoff/success, hotplug, fake
    logind transitions and SIGTERM lock survival; see NEWS.org for the exact
    coverage and its limits.
  * Release tooling, a PAM policy sample and ASan/UBSan coverage were added.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.20.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The screen locker uses the compositor's ext-session-lock-v1 protocol when
    available, so other clients cannot cover it and the session stays locked
    if the shell process dies.  The layer-shell overlay remains the documented
    fallback for compositors without the protocol.
  * AT-SPI menus follow live application tree changes, and the Guix expression
    evaluates again.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.19.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The bar's battery indicator auto-detects the first pack the kernel
    reports, so machines with BAT1 no longer hide it; the fallback bar has a
    battery too.
  * Buttons use the cursor theme's pointer cursor, including buttons inside
    menus and popovers.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0100

whelk (0.19.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * AT-SPI global menus, Scheme modules, per-monitor bars and a fail-closed
    PAM screen locker.  Golden-image tests render a real bar on a headless
    Broadway display and diff its pixels.
  * Desktop widgets are visible again: preference changes no longer replace
    the configured widget list with the empty default.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The documented bar is the built-in bar: scheme/whelk/defaults.scm holds it,
    the global menu sits after the focused window, and the example settings
    cannot drift from the fallback.
  * The global menu no longer frees the app info's own action list, which
    crashed a bar with the default module set.
  * The machine-menu glyph is drawn in the icon font instead of the text face.
  * The suite passes where /bin/sh and /bin/true do not exist.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.3.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The X11 dock fallback works on a real X server: no GLib assertion, struts
    that match the painted bar, positions taken from the window, and the four
    value _NET_WM_STRUT written too.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Session detection asks the compositor when no variable names one, so a bar
    started by a service unit or a login shell keeps its window and menu modules.
  * The detected session, and what proved it, is logged once at startup.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Nix expression runs the Guile theme test too, and refuses to package a
    tree that already carries a build directory.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A session layer: niri, sway and X11 each answer "what is in front" and
    "close it" in their own way, and the focused window, the global menu and
    its shortcuts work on all three.
  * An X11 dock fallback: a bar reserves its edge with EWMH struts.
  * Graceful degradation where layer-shell is missing (GNOME Wayland): surfaces
    are ordinary windows and the launcher, panels and notifications still work.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A macOS-shaped bar: the shell's own menu and a global menu that reads an
    application's menubar over D-Bus and synthesizes one when it exports none.
  * Bar themes: era-inspired and community palettes, brand-free names.
  * The launcher searches every file and folder under $HOME, caches and
    repositories skipped, ranked by name and path.
  * A vertical bar keeps its last group on screen and reserves the width it
    paints.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:10:00 +0100

whelk (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: bars on any edge with status, media, system and tray
    modules; a launcher with app, window, run, calc, file, web and menu modes;
    an org.freedesktop.Notifications daemon with toasts and a notification
    centre; and a Wi-Fi and Bluetooth panel whose typed password replaces the
    saved key without ever appearing on a command line.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000
